        "About one Ghanaian in ten carries hepatitis B, most infected at birth or in early childhood when chronicity is 90 per cent, through blood, sexual and perinatal routes but never food, water, utensils or hugging; it is silent for decades until cirrhosis or liver cancer; HBsAg means infection, anti-HBs immunity, anti-HBc exposure and HBeAg or high DNA active replication.",
